    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (74.26) anchors our lineup as the premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Martinez. Despite a slight park penalty, his elite ability to contribute across the board\u2014including stolen base potential\u2014makes him indispensable. He is joined at the top of our efficiency rankings by **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.51), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against RHP Johnson and Elder, respectively. **Arraez** is a lock due to his prime leadoff spot and a wind-aided environment, while **Beavers** capitalizes on an elite 16% park factor boost, making him a high-upside start for speed and R.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Bryce Harper** (55.05) out of the starting nine. While **Harper** remains a superstar, his efficiency score was depressed by a difficult matchup against the southpaw Weathers, coupled with a -13% SP skill drag that pushed him behind the likes of **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.85) and **Daulton Varsho** (60.97). We are prioritizing the platoon advantages held by **Jonathan Aranda** and **Lee** against their respective right-handed opponents. While **Gleyber Torres** and **Lawrence Butler** remained in the conversation, their negative platoon adjustments and lower-tier lineup slots kept them comfortably on the bench. \n\nWe are monitoring the bottom of our order closely; **Cal Raleigh** (46.33) and **Yainer Diaz** (45.97) are operating near our threshold for starting, largely due to the skill of opposing arms Eovaldi and Burke. Should any of the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses shift to unfavorable late-inning adjustments, we remain prepared to pivot, but for now, the data suggests this optimal configuration maximizes our output while maintaining our necessary game-cap discipline. **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Kyle Karros** remain solid pivots in the infield, providing enough stability to avoid the \"Below floor\" zone while waiting for our high-upside outfielders to capitalize on their favorable park factors.",
